  "body": "## What changed\n\nA tool had no number of its own: the post wrote `T`/`H` as the tool's 1-based **position** in the document's tool list. On the contributor's 770MX the cutter is T31 in PathPilot's tool table, but the program said `T1 M6` / `G43 H1`. It applied tool 1's length and ran about 1.5 in high. That failed safe, but a shorter H1 would have cut too deep.\n\n- **`ToolDef` gains `number: Option<u32>`.** `ChangeTool` keeps it (apply and undo); `DeleteTool` and `DeleteEntity` restore it on undo.\n- **New `SetToolNumber` command** sets or clears it, undoably. It refuses:\n  - an unknown or non-tool name;\n  - a number outside 1–99999 (0 means \"no tool\" on most controls);\n  - a number another tool already has;\n  - a no-op.\n- **Project file:** an optional `\"number\"` on the tool record, written only when set. Absent means unnumbered, which is what every older file means, so there's no version step. A stated number outside 1–99999 is refused on load, by name.\n- **`app::tool_numbers`** holds the one numbering rule used by the post: a tool's **own number**, otherwise its **list position**, so unnumbered documents post exactly as before and no golden moves. It also holds the **clash rule**: when two tools of one program would post the same number (for example an explicit 2 and another tool sitting at position 2), the post refuses and names both. With an ATC, `T2 M6` for two tools loads one of them for both.\n- **Tool editor:** a \"Tool number (0 = list position)\" field. *Apply* or *Add tool* queues a `SetToolNumber` when it changed, as its own undoable command. The `egui_tool_editor` snapshot is updated (reviewed: only the new field is added).\n\nRenumbering doesn't make operations stale: their stamps digest the tool's geometry, and the number doesn't change any path.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick` (batch mode) on f441d38. Clippy with `-D warnings`: clean. geometry, cl, tools, post and sim: ok. All the new and touched tests pass. Failures that also occur on this branch's upstream base (c9a9fb3) without the change:\n  - motion: `rotary_dflat::a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement`, plus `swarf_pose_continuity`'s two tests;\n  - app: `drilling_cross_box` / `drilling_cross_spindle` (#151);\n  - ui: the three headless-GPU tests (no fallback graphics adapter on this macOS machine).\n- Merges cleanly with current `upstream/main`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `tool_numbers::a_number_is_set_cleared_and_walked_by_undo_and_redo`\n- `tool_numbers::bad_numbers_are_refused_by_name`\n- `tool_numbers::change_and_delete_keep_the_number`\n- `tool_numbers::the_post_writes_a_tools_own_number_and_positions_for_the_rest` (T31 and H31 through the default post)\n- `tool_numbers::two_tools_posting_one_number_refuse_by_name`\n- `tool_numbers::the_project_file_carries_the_number_and_only_when_set`\n- `egui_app::tool_number_tests::setting_a_tool_number_is_a_command_with_undo`\n- `egui_app::tool_number_tests::the_editor_draft_shows_the_tools_own_number`\n- `egui_app::tests::tool_editor_snapshot` (updated image)\n\nChangelog: Tools can carry their controller tool number (tool editor), which the post writes as T/H; unnumbered tools still post as their list position, and two tools posting one number are refused\n\nFixes #221\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
